  "reading": "MATCH, uninformative beyond replication: both arms optimal on every item, no abstention, refutation or wrong answer; the independent rescoring agrees with the primary scoring on the genome's and the routed composition's plans and on every item's truth, and no secondary arm's rescoring disagrees; the expected tie, which replicates admission v3's DEFAULT verdict on real items and is not a new capability",
  "rule": "flow_expansion_mcf MATCHES the routed composition on F7's held-out items when all four conditions hold and the comparator replicates v4. (1) NO_WRONG_ANSWER: no held-out item is scored wrong for flow_expansion_mcf; wrong is run_v4.f7_score's 'wrong' (over budget, out of bounds or a flow claim the recomputation contradicts) or a receipt the independent verifier REFUTED, which is scored wrong whatever its plan, as admission v3 scores a refuted answer. (2) GENOME_DECIDES_EVERY_ITEM: no held-out item is scored no_decision for the genome (an abstention of any kind, or an output f7_score cannot read as a plan). (3) NOT_SIGNIFICANTLY_WORSE: the one-sided exact sign test over discordant items gives p >= 0.05 for 'the genome is worse'. A loss is an item where routed is optimal and the genome is not, or where the genome is scored no_decision and routed is not (routed returned a plan, even a wrong one); a win is an item where the genome is optimal and routed is not; every other item is a tie, so the count is asymmetric against the genome. (4) LATENCY_WITHIN_RATIO: the genome's median latency over the held-out items is at most 1.25x the routed composition's, both end to end through greg.cognition.cortex.reason on this machine. Outcome: INCONCLUSIVE when the independent rescoring disagrees with the primary scoring on any genome or routed plan or on any item's truth, except on the plan of a genome receipt the verifier REFUTED (the refutation scores that row wrong whatever its plan scores, so it decides NO_WRONG_ANSWER); a disagreement on a secondary arm (compiled, PMCF) is reported, makes the run informative and does not change the outcome; otherwise NO_MATCH, naming every failed condition, when a condition fails, except that a failure of LATENCY_WITHIN_RATIO alone is INCONCLUSIVE when the comparator did not replicate; otherwise INCONCLUSIVE when the comparator did not replicate v4 (routed optimal on every held-out item); otherwise MATCH. INVALID_RUN replaces the outcome when an integrity check fails; the measured outcome is kept beside it. The thresholds are admission v3's DEFAULT rule's (alpha 0.05, 1.25x); the rule deviates from that rule in the ways DEVIATIONS lists."
 },
