  "rule": "F7_LIFT_WITH_GENOME (secondary; it does not change v4's frozen verdict, LIFT): v4's F7 rule, verbatim 'F7 (natural instances, exact truth): routed optimal > best constituent optimal, routed wrong <= best constituent wrong, one-sided exact sign test over discordant held-out items p < 0.05, routed median latency <= 60 s and <= 10x the best constituent's median. Best constituent chosen on held-out results (most optimal, then fewest wrong). Practitioner, compiled-arm and per-network comparisons reported, not part of the rule. VPL = families meeting their rule.', re-evaluated with the constituent set v4's two constituents (graph_alone_greedy, optimize_flow_blind: their optimal and wrong counts on the same items, as v4's frozen evidence records them, which do not depend on the machine) plus flow_expansion_mcf from this run, with routed being this run's routed_composition. The best constituent is chosen as v4 chooses it (most optimal, then fewest wrong; a full tie keeps v4's order, so a v4 constituent precedes the genome). When the genome is the best constituent, five conditions are read from this run's genome and routed rows (one machine): (1) ROUTED_MORE_OPTIMAL: routed optimal > the genome's optimal; (2) ROUTED_NO_MORE_WRONG: routed wrong <= the genome's wrong; (3) SIGN_TEST_P_BELOW_ALPHA: over the discordant items (routed optimal and the genome not is a routed win, the reverse a routed loss) the one-sided exact sign test for 'routed is better' gives p < 0.05; (4) ROUTED_MEDIAN_WITHIN_CHAIN_BUDGET: routed median latency <= 60 s; (5) ROUTED_MEDIAN_WITHIN_MULTIPLIER: routed median latency <= 10x the genome's median (medians of the recorded seconds rounded to 4 decimals, as run_v4 rounds them). LIFT when all five hold, otherwise NO_LIFT naming every failed condition. INCONCLUSIVE instead when the rows are not exactly the items v4's counts cover; when the independent rescoring disagrees with the primary scoring on a genome or routed plan or a truth (with the primary rule's exception for a refuted genome receipt); or when a v4 constituent is the best constituent: its paired rows and latencies are v4's, from another run on another machine, so the sign test and the latency conditions cannot be computed from this run's rows, and v4's verdict against it stands. A REFUTED genome receipt counts as wrong here, as in the primary rule; v4 scored its constituents through run_v4.op(), which counted a receipt in any state but NONE as no decision, so a refutation weighs against the genome in ROUTED_NO_MORE_WRONG and in the wrong-count tie-break where v4's scoring would not (v4's held-out constituent counts hold no such receipt). INVALID_RUN replaces the outcome when an integrity check fails.",
